FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-great-wall.
FILED BY: the high command, which favors piecemeal construction.

OFF THE RECORD: The wall is built piecemeal: crews raise scattered
OFF THE RECORD: sections, and the gaps are filled in later, or never.
OFF THE RECORD: This case tallies the sections with the standard
OFF THE RECORD: statutes (enact them first: trial enact --canon).
OFF THE RECORD: Incorporating the statutes of schedules incorporates,
OFF THE RECORD: transitively, the statutes of arithmetic they stand on.

INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-schedules.
INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-strings.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sections IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING 500 AND 200 AND 350 AND 125.
    PROCLAIM "sections reported: " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE LENGTH OF sections.
    PROCLAIM "li completed: " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE FINDING OF total-of REGARDING sections.
    PROCLAIM "longest section: " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE FINDING OF greatest-of REGARDING sections.
    PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF repetition REGARDING "so the wall grows. " AND 3.
    SHOULD THE FINDING OF containment-of REGARDING sections AND 0 EQUAL SUSTAINED, PROCLAIM "an idle crew has been reported to the high command.". FAILING WHICH, PROCLAIM "no crew stands idle. The command is pleased, provisionally.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
